  | &#8220;
  = @pg_title
  | &#8221;

markdown:
  *LP-12* is a series of twelve pictures, each to do with some aspect of record
  collecting.

  I started making this series in 2009, when vinyl LPs were an anachronistic
  minority interest. Today, records are a collectible commodity, fashion accessory, and the 
  object of much fetishization. That cultural shift changed the tone of
  the work as it progressed.

  The paintings, each the size of a 12" LP sleeve, are like tracks in an
  album.  They all use the same palette (instruments), and each is a
  self-contained whole, but sympathetic to its
  companions.

  Every painting makes reference to a
  different artistic movement, and they all have an epigram etched into their
  surface, in the way messages are often scratched into the run-out grooves of
  records.

table#pic_block
  -@links.sort_by{|h| h[:fpath]}.each_slice(6).with_index do |row, i|
    tr
      td 
        '#{i + 1 }.
    tr
      - row.each do |cell|
        td
          a(href="/piece/series/lp-12/#{cell[:fpath]}")
            img src="/i/thumbs/#{cell[:image]}" alt=cell[:title]
